<rss version="2.0" xmlns:atom="http://www.w3.org/2005/Atom" xmlns:media="http://search.yahoo.com/mrss/" xmlns:dc="http://purl.org/dc/elements/1.1/"><channel><language>en</language><title>Latest news from the Middle East, daily international news reports - France 24</title><description>FRANCE 24’s coverage and analyses of political and social issues across the Middle East, including Egypt, the Gulf states, Iraq, Israel, Jordan, Lebanon, Saudi Arabia, Syria, Yemen and beyond.</description><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/</link><lastBuildDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 18:28:02 GMT</lastBuildDate><atom:link href="https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/rss" rel="self" type="application/rss+xml"/><item><category>Tête à tête</category><title>'We were naive' about Hamas, Israeli ex-hostage Shoshan Haran says</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/tv-shows/t%C3%AAte-%C3%A0-t%C3%AAte/20261006-we-were-naive-about-hamas-israeli-ex-hostage-shoshan-haran-says</link><description>
In an interview with FRANCE 24, Israeli former hostage Shoshan Haran said "we were naive" about Hamas before the October 7, 2023 attack on her kibbutz. Held in Gaza for 50 days, she recalled refusing to "show weakness" to her captors. She also called the accusations of genocide against Israel "a lie" and shared her late husband's last words.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7cb8caa-c0bf-11f1-ac40-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/MONTAGE-SHOSHAN-HARAN.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f7cb8caa-c0bf-11f1-ac40-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/MONTAGE-SHOSHAN-HARAN.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1f7defb8-be59-11f1-b751-855272092b6e</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 15:01:53 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>Marc PERELMAN</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Israel warns Gazans will pay 'heavy price' for any October 7 attacks on military</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261006-israel-warns-gazans-will-pay-heavy-price-for-any-october-7-attacks-on-military</link><description>
Israel on Tuesday said that Hamas and the Palestinian population in Gaza would pay a "heavy price" if any of Israel's armed forces were harmed on the three-year anniversary of the militant group's October 7 attack. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe623a8-c158-11f1-ab65-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278512155571.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe623a8-c158-11f1-ab65-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278512155571.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">d6ce7df2-c158-11f1-aa3b-77497fb40820</guid><pubDate>Tue, 06 Oct 2026 07:50:10 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9fe623a8-c158-11f1-ab65-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26278512155571.jpg">© Oded Balilty, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Saudi-backed Yemeni forces expel the Houthis from several areas around key strait, officials say</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/saudi-backed-yemeni-forces-expel-the-houthis-from-several-areas-around-key-strait-officials-say</link><description>
Saudi-backed Yemeni government forces staged a lightning advance on ​Monday to retake the coast around the Bab el-Mandeb Strait up to the city of Mocha, the government said, pushing the Iran-backed Houthis out of most of the areas they seized last month. FRANCE 24's Monte Francis reports.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06e24072-c0f1-11f1-8ede-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4580563926ac3f725bc3d82-10617721.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/06e24072-c0f1-11f1-8ede-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/capture-4580563926ac3f725bc3d82-10617721.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">974c9294-c0f0-11f1-9f81-71ed274b3f93</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 19:17:05 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>ISIS suspects face 'outsourced' justice in Iraq as HRW warns of 'collective global detention crisis'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261005-isis-suspects-face-outsourced-justice-in-iraq-as-hrw-warns-of-collective-global-detention-crisis-1</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Letta Tayler, Senior Counterterrorism Advisor at Human Rights Watch. She warns of the detention of suspected Islamic State members transferred from northeast Syria to Iraq as part of a much wider "global detention crisis". The men and boys now held in Iraq are living in 'dire' conditions, including deaths from illness, allegations of torture, and serious questions surrounding access to effective legal representation. Can accountability be achieved through legal proceedings that respect the rule of law and provide genuine justice to both detainees and victims?
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f0c0f28-c0cb-11f1-abfc-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-151326-152657-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/1f0c0f28-c0cb-11f1-abfc-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261005-151326-152657-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">2424c5e0-c0cb-11f1-834e-a9d28765d43a</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 15:46:33 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis claim attacks on Riyadh airport as Saudi-led forces strike Yemen</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261005-yemen-military-announces-broad-range-of-strikes-against-houthis-in-bid-to-retake-lost-territory</link><description>
Iran-backed Houthis said Monday they had struck Riyadh's international airport and an Aramco refinery as Saudi-led forces intensified attacks on Houthi positions in Yemen in a bid to retake territory. Pakistan and Turkey also pledged troops to Saudi Arabia under a new defence pact. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3df66fda-c091-11f1-a1a7-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265728988880.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3df66fda-c091-11f1-a1a7-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265728988880.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">70aafcd4-c091-11f1-9280-d31aef42a17f</guid><pubDate>Mon, 05 Oct 2026 08:12:54 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/3df66fda-c091-11f1-a1a7-578a4b968fd6/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26265728988880.jpg">© Ansar Allah Media Office via AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Iran says no military solution to war as peace talks with US stall</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-iran-us-military-middle-east-war-peace-talks</link><description>
Iran's diplomat said on Sunday there was no military solution to the US war against Iran as peace talks appeared stalled. Washington has scaled back attacks in favour of economic pressure, while Iran's attempted Hormuz blockade remains contentious. A UK maritime agency reported another tanker hit by an unidentified projectile.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff0fd15a-bfcb-11f1-9bd3-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26179355008979.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff0fd15a-bfcb-11f1-9bd3-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26179355008979.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">461c92c6-c03b-11f1-b751-6586f6241841</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 21:41:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/ff0fd15a-bfcb-11f1-9bd3-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26179355008979.jpg">© AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>The week in pictures: Disaster averted on Flydubai flight, French school protests and Bangkok floods</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-the-week-in-pictures-disaster-averted-flydubai-flight-french-school-protests-and-bangkok-floods</link><description>
From French highschoolers protesting to demand better learning conditions to a Flydubai flight diverted to Saudi Arabia after a flightcrew member's onboard attack and flooded streets in Bangkok, FRANCE 24 looks back at the week's most striking pictures.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29936e26-bf10-11f1-9557-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273599274856-1-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29936e26-bf10-11f1-9557-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273599274856-1-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">36b64d56-bf1c-11f1-acdf-6701c49d00b5</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 13:35:11 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/29936e26-bf10-11f1-9557-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273599274856-1-1.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Yemen's government declares counter-offensive as Houthis cut vital route to besieged city</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-yemen-leader-announces-counter-offensive-as-houthis-cut-off-supply-route-besieged-city-taiz</link><description>
The ​leader of ​Yemen's Saudi-backed government announced the beginning of a ​major ‌military ⁠operation against the Iran-backed Houthis ‌on Sunday aimed at ⁠recapturing territory under their control. The announcement came as Houthi forces cut off a vital supply route to the besieged government-held city of Taiz, according to several security sources.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c14ee92e-c08d-11f1-b754-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T135414Z-2043951740-RC2DWNA2JWYI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c14ee92e-c08d-11f1-b754-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T135414Z-2043951740-RC2DWNA2JWYI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8f53ebc8-bff1-11f1-91cc-b955e607a27f</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 12:59:17 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c14ee92e-c08d-11f1-b754-dd51fcab6130/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-04T135414Z-2043951740-RC2DWNA2JWYI-RTRMADP-3-IRAN-CRISIS-YEMEN-1.jpg">© via REUTERS - Yemen News Agency</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>West Bank: Palestinians ‘harassed’ by settlers’ increasing use of drones</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-occupied-west-bank-palestinians-harassed-settlers-drones</link><description>
Palestinians and activists report an increased use of drones in the occupied West Bank, particularly by the army and settlers, to whom the government supplies the drones directly. The drones are used to intimidate, monitor, demolish and make daily life unbearable.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad046c8-bd7a-11f1-b57d-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Pic-Drones.png"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad046c8-bd7a-11f1-b57d-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Pic-Drones.png" type="image/png" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">72da03b6-be74-11f1-bf6c-41e1b8a52073</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 12:01:27 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9ad046c8-bd7a-11f1-b57d-d367a0468893/w:1024/p:16x9/Cover-Pic-Drones.png">© The Observers / Herd of Justice</source><dc:creator>Marguerite Ipek LACROIX</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Israel prepares to mark October 7</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/israel-prepares-to-mark-october-7</link><description>
An Israeli strike on a civilian vehicle in Gaza on Sunday killed one Palestinian and wounded at least 11 others. Israel’s military said it was targeting a Hamas militant. Palestinians have reported a surge in Israeli fire and airstrikes across Gaza over the past month, with more than 75,000 people killed and much of the enclave destroyed. Meanwhile, Israelis held their weekly protest in Tel Aviv’s Hostages Square, the last before Wednesday marks three years since the October 7 attack. Protesters said they wanted to commemorate the victims and demand an independent state inquiry into the events and decisions that led to the attack. The Hamas-led assault killed around 1,200 people in Israel and saw more than 250 others taken hostage, according to Israeli authorities. Rachael Goldberg Polin, an American-Israeli activist and mother of slain hostage Hersh Goldberg-Polin, speaks to France 24.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9482b6e4-bfe0-11f1-9696-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-120715-121646-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/9482b6e4-bfe0-11f1-9696-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-120715-121646-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">99316d34-bfe0-11f1-8d20-8fa7ddd26abe</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 10:59:38 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Who are the mystery pilots who successfully landed endangered Flydubai flight 1073?</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261004-who-are-the-mystery-pilots-who-successfully-landed-endangered-flydubai-flight-1073</link><description>
A passenger on Flydubai flight 1073 has described the actions of on-duty crew members who rushed into the cockpit to stabilise and land the plane after the co-pilot attacked the captain with a crash axe. The flight carrying 182 people en route to Israel Wednesday was able to make an emergency landing in Saudi Arabia after a descent so extreme that part of its rudder was torn away. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da1105dc-bfcf-11f1-8542-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273485606536-1.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da1105dc-bfcf-11f1-8542-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273485606536-1.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">8218d5c8-bfcd-11f1-a3ed-df9ae4e03873</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 09:36:47 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/da1105dc-bfcf-11f1-8542-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/AP26273485606536-1.jpg">© Ariel Schalit, AP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>Yemen’s Houthis claim attacks on Aramco facilities in Riyadh</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/yemen-s-houthis-claim-attacks-on-aramco-facilities-in-riyadh</link><description>
Yemen’s Houthi rebels have claimed responsibility for attacks in Riyadh, including on facilities belonging to Aramco, the world’s largest oil company. This follows reports from residents of flames and smoke rising from an oil facility on the outskirts of the Saudi capital. Meanwhile, the Houthis have accused Saudi Arabia of launching dozens of strikes on Sanaa, warning that they will continue to respond to any escalation with further escalation. Here’s Jennie Shin with more on the situation on the ground.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f23d5188-bfca-11f1-bb16-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-090624-090759-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/f23d5188-bfca-11f1-bb16-1ff0321dbbd3/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20261004-090624-090759-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">f759acd4-bfca-11f1-b895-5fa848c9c018</guid><pubDate>Sun, 04 Oct 2026 08:21:37 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Houthis claim strike on oil facilty near Riyadh, accuse Saudi forces of pounding Yemen's capital</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-houthis-blame-saudi-air-strikes-loud-blasts-rock-yemen-capital-sanaa</link><description>
Houthi rebels accused Saudi forces of launching 26 strikes on Sanaa on Saturday after loud explosions rocked the Yemeni capital. The Iran-backed group said it struck an oil facility south of Riyadh, where flames and a large plume of smoke were seen rising from a plant belonging to oil giant Aramco.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84e4ed72-bf65-11f1-8c8d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D26B6KC.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84e4ed72-bf65-11f1-8c8d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D26B6KC.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">9ffb3a26-bf33-11f1-a8eb-b11ec008a238</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 14:31:30 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/84e4ed72-bf65-11f1-8c8d-13420ab900a2/w:1024/p:16x9/000-D26B6KC.jpg">© AFP</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>UAE investigators say Omani Flydubai co-pilot was planning 'terrorist' attack</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261003-co-pilot-on-flydubai-flight-was-banned-from-flying-by-oman-for-holding-extremist-views</link><description>
The Omani co-pilot accused of attacking the captain aboard a Flydubai flight to Israel on September 30 attempted to carry out a "terrorist" attack, the United Arab Emirates prosecutor general said ​Saturday. The alleged assailant, identified as Omani national Hamam al-Hammami, had been barred from flying in his country due to his radical ideological views, several media reported.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c016f272-bcd7-11f1-b2a8-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T135141Z-62230240-RC2PTNASHNVV-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-GULF-FLIGHT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c016f272-bcd7-11f1-b2a8-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T135141Z-62230240-RC2PTNASHNVV-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-GULF-FLIGHT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">0b3780cc-bef0-11f1-9a19-61bc17c7209b</guid><pubDate>Sat, 03 Oct 2026 06:17:45 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/c016f272-bcd7-11f1-b2a8-ddce071186a9/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-09-30T135141Z-62230240-RC2PTNASHNVV-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-GULF-FLIGHT.jpg">© Ammar Awad, Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Netanyahu warns of 'very heavy price' if any country found to be behind FlyDubai incident</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-netanyahu-warns-of-very-heavy-price-if-any-country-found-to-be-behind-flydubai-incident</link><description>
Israeli Prime Minister Benjamin Netanyahu on Friday warned that any country or organisation found to be responsible for the violent clash on board an Israel-bound FlyDubai flight would "pay a very heavy price". While Netanyahu has alleged the co-pilot who stabbed his captain mid-flight had undergone "Islamist radicalisation", the motive behind the incident remains unclear.
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc04bcc8-be62-11f1-8da5-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-01T033528Z-264219572-RC23UNADFHPE-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-GULF-FLIGHT.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc04bcc8-be62-11f1-8da5-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-01T033528Z-264219572-RC23UNADFHPE-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-GULF-FLIGHT.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">1fc81f22-be66-11f1-833b-9d8df2a477b6</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 13:55:35 GMT</pubDate><source url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/bc04bcc8-be62-11f1-8da5-69fad0a7cb9f/w:1024/p:16x9/2026-10-01T033528Z-264219572-RC23UNADFHPE-RTRMADP-3-ISRAEL-GULF-FLIGHT.jpg">© GPO via Reuters</source><dc:creator>FRANCE 24</dc:creator></item><item><category></category><title>'America is leaving Iraq, but Iran isn't: Withdrawal a massive strategic and tactical mistake'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/video/20261002-america-is-leaving-iraq-but-iran-isn-t-withdrawal-a-massive-strategic-and-tactical-mistake-1</link><description>
Erin Ogunkeye is pleased to welcome Bamo Nouri, investigative journalist and also Honorary Research Fellow with the Department of International Politics at City Saint George's University of London. He sees the end of the American military presence in Iraq as a profound shift in the balance of power inside the country. For him, the central question is not whether Iraq has formally regained sovereignty, but whether it possesses the political cohesion, security capacity and economic independence necessary to exercise that sovereignty. 
</description><media:thumbnail url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b594de52-be41-11f1-a230-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-150850-151852-CS.jpg"/><enclosure url="https://s.france24.com/media/display/b594de52-be41-11f1-a230-13e372f41e70/w:1024/p:16x9/EN-20260930-150850-151852-CS.jpg" type="image/jpeg" length="0"/><guid isPermaLink="false">bacf31ec-be41-11f1-b5dd-e1da7f6cd34b</guid><pubDate>Fri, 02 Oct 2026 10:11:15 GMT</pubDate><dc:creator>FRANCE24</dc:creator></item><item><category>Middle East</category><title>Flydubai hero pilot tells Modi 'I could not let all those people die'</title><link>https://www.france24.com/en/middle-east/20261002-flydubai-hero-pilot-tells-modi-i-could-not-let-all-those-people-die</link><description>
Smit Machchhar, the Indian captain who was attacked by his co-pilot onboard the Flydubai flight 1073 in an apparent attempt to crash the plane, on Friday told Prime Minister Narendra Modi that although he was severely injured in the altercation, “I could not let all those people die”. Although collapsed, he made a last-ditch effort and managed to push the door to the cockpit open.
